    "created_at": "2025-01-20T12:04:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-20T12:05:09Z",
    "body": "> When would we not want to allow numbers? Numbers seem good to allow. I think we only want two types.\n\nArguably, it's very easy to pass epoch-based timestamps to functions/properties that accept monotonic timestamps, resulting in nonsensical outcomes. Not sure this means we should disallow number-based timestamps in future APIs, but it's at the very least a legit thing to consider.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
