    "created_at": "2025-01-21T20:19:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-21T20:19:33Z",
    "body": "Numbers are easily confused between instants and durations. Sometimes you can name the method or field to be clear which it expects, but, for example, `setTimeout()` isn't named that way.  [Not everyone even measures time in milliseconds.](https://github.com/w3ctag/design-principles/issues/344#issuecomment-938352123) There's a consistency argument in https://github.com/w3ctag/design-principles/issues/425 that we should accept the resulting bugs, but I'd rather that future APIs restrict themselves to more precise types instead.\n\nTemporal doesn't have a type to represent \"timestamps\" on the monotonic clock, so those have to be [Durations](https://tc39.es/proposal-temporal/docs/duration.html) (generally from the [time origin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-settings-object-time-origin), but [`performance.timeOrigin`, which expresses that instant to JS, is itself a duration](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dom-performance-timeorigin)). I think most of these are returned from methods rather than passed to them, and we can't change existing return types without breaking backward compatibility.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
